statement:
Let $X$ be a topological space. A \textbf{presheaf} $\mathcal{F}$ of rings on $X$ assigns to each open set $U \subseteq X$ a ring $\mathcal{F}(U)$, and to each inclusion $V \subseteq U$ a restriction homomorphism $\operatorname{res}_{U,V} \colon \mathcal{F}(U) \to \mathcal{F}(V)$, such that:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\operatorname{res}_{U,U} = \operatorname{id}_{\mathcal{F}(U)}$.
        \item If $W \subseteq V \subseteq U$, then $\operatorname{res}_{U,W} = \operatorname{res}_{V,W} \circ \operatorname{res}_{U,V}$.
    \end{enumerate}
